To handle long text professionally, we should avoid large blocks of plain text and instead use a typography-first approach. Since you are using styled-components (implied by LoginStyles), we will create a refined HeroSection wrapper and update the subtext to use a more readable line height and letter spacing.
1. New Styled Components
Add these to your LoginStyles.js or at the top of your LoginPort.js file. These focus on professional spacing, subtle color contrast, and a "Modern Enterprise" look.
import { styled } from "@mui/material/styles";
import { Typography, Box } from "@mui/material";

// A wrapper to give the text more breathing room and a professional alignment
export const HeroTextWrapper = styled(Box)(({ theme }) => ({
  display: "flex",
  flexDirection: "column",
  gap: theme.spacing(2),
  maxWidth: "520px", // Prevents the text from stretching too wide (improves readability)
  marginBottom: theme.spacing(4),
}));

export const MainTitle = styled(Typography)(({ theme }) => ({
  fontSize: "2.2rem",
  fontWeight: 700,
  lineHeight: 1.2,
  color: "#ffffff", // Pure white for high contrast on dark bg
  letterSpacing: "-0.02em",
  textShadow: "0px 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.2)",
}));

export const DescriptionText = styled(Typography)(({ theme }) => ({
  fontSize: "1.05rem",
  lineHeight: 1.6,
  color: "rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8)", // Slightly muted for hierarchy
  fontWeight: 400,
  borderLeft: `3px solid ${theme.palette.primary.main}`, // Accent line for professional look
  paddingLeft: theme.spacing(2),
}));

2. Implementation in your JSX
Replace the current two lines of text in the LEFT COLUMN section of your LoginPort component with this structured layout:
{/* LEFT COLUMN */}
<LeftCol>
  <HeroTextWrapper>
    <MainTitle variant="h1">
      {content?.hero?.welcomeTitle}
    </MainTitle>
    <DescriptionText>
      {content?.hero?.subText}
    </DescriptionText>
  </HeroTextWrapper>

  <BigHeading>{content?.legal?.title}</BigHeading>
  <FeatureList>
    {/* ... rest of your legal items ... */}
  </FeatureList>
</LeftCol>

Key Design Enhancements:
 * Max-Width Constraint: By limiting the width to 520px, the eye doesn't have to travel as far, making long sentences much easier to scan.
 * Visual Hierarchy: The MainTitle is bold and heavy, while the DescriptionText uses a softer color and a left border "accent" commonly seen in high-end FinTech dashboards.
 * Line Height: Increased to 1.6 for the description to ensure that even with "too much text," it doesn't look like a cluttered wall of words.
